NOTE TO OPERATOR (this is not valid JSON — strip this block before using).

This template needs ~25 hand-labelled cases. Suggested coverage:

  Direction-positive cases (~10):
    - 3 from KXTRUMP* series (varied subtopics: Iran, China, immigration)
    - 2 from KXFISA / legislation series
    - 2 from KXMOC* / political-event series
    - 3 from sources that are NOT Reuters/Al Jazeera/AP (the eval should
      not over-fit on top-tier wires)

  Direction-negative cases (~5):
    - Headlines that suggest the market resolves NO (talks scrapped,
      bill killed, deal cancelled).
    - Cover both Trump-administration and non-administration actors.

  Direction-neutral cases (~10):
    - Headlines that mention market entities but are NOT new information
      (rhetoric, opposition figures, speculation, recap pieces) —
      these are the cases the LLM should correctly classify as
      magnitude=none.
    - Include at least 2 “Trump-token false positive” headlines (ones
      that should match KXTRUMPENDORSE / KXPARDONSTRUMP etc. by token
      overlap but are about unrelated Trump activity) — these are the
      PROFIT-MATCH-001 long-tail cases the eval should catch.

  Edge cases (~5):
    - 1 headline in non-English (or with extensive emoji) — robustness check.
    - 1 satire or opinion headline (the LLM should classify as
      neutral/none even if it mentions the market entity).
    - 1 very short headline (≤8 words).
    - 1 very long headline (≥30 words).
    - 1 numeric-data headline (poll result, stock price) — these often
      misclassify as small/moderate when the actual signal is none.

After labelling, rename this file to operator_labelled_25.json (drop the
.template extension and remove the NOTE TO OPERATOR block above) and run:

  .venv/bin/python scripts/llm_eval.py --model qwen2.5:7b --cases tests/fixtures/llm_eval_cases/operator_labelled_25.json
  .venv/bin/python scripts/llm_eval.py --model qwen3:14b --cases tests/fixtures/llm_eval_cases/operator_labelled_25.json

Compare the two reports in logs/eval/ to inform the PROFIT-LLM-001
unification decision (or any future model upgrade).
